    "finding": "No simple structure-only descriptor (crosslink density, ring-atom fraction, aromatic fraction, rotatable-bond density) predicts DGEBA-amine network Tg out-of-sample on the chemically-diverse rights-clean set. Best LOO MAE (40.5 C, ring_only) does NOT beat the trivial NULL mean-Tg baseline (31.8 C).",
    "implication": "This is not fixable by swapping to a different single whole-molecule descriptor on n=7 (that would be post-hoc fishing). A trustworthy network-Tg model needs a TOPOLOGICAL backbone-rigidity-between-crosslinks descriptor (rigid-fragment fraction on the junction-to-junction path), validated on n>=12 rights-clean systems. That is the concrete next step; it is future work, not claimed here.",
    "root_cause": "Tg is governed by rigidity of the units that sit IN the network backbone BETWEEN crosslink junctions, which a whole-molecule ring/aromatic count cannot resolve: it cannot distinguish backbone-rigid aromatics from pendant or flexibly-CH2-linked aromatics, nor rigid from flexible (chair) rings."
  },
  "honest_limitations": [
    "n=7 unique rights-clean systems is still below the n>=12 Phase-0 data gate (G1); this run advances the data count but the model is REFUTED, so promotion is further away, not closer.",
    "Literature ground truth carries a MEASURED inter-lab scatter of ~10 C std / 20 C range (DGEBA/DDS across 3 labs), which caps achievable MAE regardless of model quality.",
    "Cure schedule and DSC onset-vs-midpoint conventions differ across S1/S2/S3; leave-one-source-out is reported precisely to expose this method heterogeneity.",
    "With n=7, a 2-descriptor linear model has limited degrees of freedom; ring-only (1 desc) is reported as the more robust variant and is not over-parameterised.",
    "Cycloaliphatic class spans 97-158 C (flexible chair ring CYDM vs sterically hindered IPDA); a flat ring-atom-fraction credit cannot separate these -- a known model weakness, stated.",
    "No wet-lab measurement, product qualification, or superiority is claimed."
  ],
