  "verdict": {
    "headline": "Network-Tg remains the highest-value UNVALIDATED coating-science gap, and this run is a RED-TEAM CORRECTION, not a promotion. It genuinely expands the rights-clean cited set from n=5 single-source to n=9 measurements / 7 unique systems across 3 INDEPENDENT sources (4 amine classes), and measures the inter-lab Tg floor directly (DGEBA/DDS = 200/204/220 C, std 8.6 C). Tested on this independent data, the v1 structure-only physics model is REFUTED: best LOO MAE 40.5 C (ring_only) is WORSE than a trivial NULL mean-Tg baseline (31.8 C) and does NOT beat the incumbent ML (39.1 C); it beats only raw Van Krevelen (109.1 C). Whole-molecule ring/aromatic fraction cannot separate backbone-rigid aromatics (DDS, Tg 208) from CH2-linked/pendant aromatics (m-XDA, Tg 100) at near-identical aromatic fraction. The v1 'ring r=+0.69, one dataset away' claim was a small-sample artifact. A trustworthy KPI needs a topological backbone-rigidity descriptor validated on n>=12; that is future work. NO Phase-0 promotion is claimed and none is warranted.",
    "phase": "PRE_PHASE_0",
    "red_team_correction_to_v1": "v1 reported ring-fraction Pearson r=+0.69 and LOO MAE ~24-29 C and framed network-Tg as 'one rights-clean dataset away from a KPI'. This run adds genuinely independent rights-clean data and REFUTES that optimism: ring correlation falls to +0.46 and best LOO MAE rises to 40.5 C, WORSE than a trivial mean-Tg baseline (31.8 C). The v1 signal was a small-sample artifact of 5 homogeneous systems. Network-Tg is FURTHER from Phase-0 than v1 implied; do not present the v1 headline to founders.",
    "status": "SIMPLE_STRUCTURE_ONLY_MODEL_REFUTED_ON_INDEPENDENT_DATA__V1_SIGNAL_WAS_SMALL_SAMPLE_ARTIFACT"
  }
